I2C master driver for the Intel chipset SMBus controller (ICH family, PIIX4)

Syntax:
    i2c-ichsmb [--u unit] [--b speed] [-i | -I irq] [-p bus:dev.func] [-s] [-t ms]
               [-U user[:group]] [-v...]

Options handled by the I2C library:
    --u unit    create /dev/i2c<unit> (default 0)
    --b speed   bus speed in Hz; only 100000 is accepted, the chipset
                runs the SMBus at a fixed clock

Driver options:
    -i          interrupt mode (default: polling). PIIX4 is polling only.
    -I irq      interrupt mode on this interrupt number instead of the one
                the PCI server reports. Needed when the PCI server's routing
                table lacks the controller, e.g. QEMU q35 (use -I 16). If no
                interrupt arrives in the first 20 transactions, the driver
                logs a warning.
    -p b:d.f    use the controller at this PCI address (hex), e.g. 0:1f.3.
                Without -p the first supported controller is used. With -p,
                untested Intel SMBus functions are treated as ICH-compatible.
    -s          reads of 3 to 33 bytes after a one-byte register use SMBus
                Block Read (the chip sends a count byte first) instead of
                I2C Block Read
    -t ms       per-transaction timeout (default 100)
    -U user     after start-up keep only the abilities the driver needs
                and run as this user (name or uid:gid). Start as root.
    -v          more logging to slog2 (repeat for more), buffer set
                i2c_ichsmb: slog2info -b i2c_ichsmb. Default: warnings and
                errors.

Examples:
    i2c-ichsmb -i -U qnxuser       interrupt mode, run as qnxuser
    i2c-ichsmb -I 16               interrupt mode on interrupt 16 (QEMU q35)
    i2c-ichsmb --u 1 -p 0:1f.3     /dev/i2c1 for the controller at 0:1f.3

Transfers the controller can express are listed in driver/core/smb_map.c.
Anything else is refused with an error rather than approximated.
